// An object type literal carrying an index signature (`[key: string]: number`)
// is a legal declaration - assignments into it honor the index value type -
// but open (wildcard) shapes were never lowered to C++ (commit 83c9503d
// refused the wildcard shape label on purpose: no C++ value spelling for open
// objects). `cp3 check` runs the entry's codegen, so a declared binding whose
// type has no spelling is CP3401, not exit 0, even when the binding is never
// read. Interfaces with the same member still spell through the wrapper.
let d: { [key: string]: number } = {};
